<title>GERMANY: Brazil says 96/97 coffee crop seen at 24 mln bags.</title>
<headline>Brazil says 96/97 coffee crop seen at 24 mln bags.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's 1996/97 coffee crop will not exceed 24 million 60-kg bags, said Luiz Marcos Suplicy Hafers, vice-chairman of the National Coffee Council of Brazil.</p>
<p>&quot;The USDA (the U.S. Department of Agriculture) said 27 million and we have also been hearing of over 30 million but I can assure you this crop won't be over 24 million,&quot; he told the F.O. Licht world coffee conference in Hamburg.</p>
<p>--Vera Eckert, Hamburg Newsroom +49 40 41903275</p>
